{"type": "assistant", "message": {"model": "claude-fable-5-2", "id": "msg_011CgvhnAg8cpgupEY8SeEqm", "type": "message", "role": "assistant", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "The own-frame H/A bias hypothesis is refuted: `b` is ≈ ±0.1–0.3 logits with inconsistent sign across chunks, so there is no constant slot bias to remove. What does exist is a frame-specific role-swap disagreement (mean |b| ≈ 0.7–0.8 logits in ambiguous frames, vs 0.25–0.4 for the y-mirror) — a non-equivariance that the view averaging already handles and that no bias-type edit can remove.\n\nOne last mechanistic hypothesis for the under-splitting: the recurrent states are too sticky (update gates `z` hold too long), so short possessions never register. If true, lowering the update-gate bias should add possessions and raise spellF1, and raising it should do the opposite. I'll test this as a two-sided sensitivity measurement in the simulator, separately for each GRU layer.\n\n```python\ndef full_logits(Wd):\n    out = {}\n    for n in NAMES:\n        X = views(D[n][\"x\"])\n        out[n] = back_end(front_end(X, Wd), Wd).astype(np.float32)\n    return out\ndef variant(edits):\n    Wd = {k: BASE[k] for k in BASE}\n    for k, fn in edits.items():\n        Wd[k] = fn(BASE[k].copy())\n    return Wd\nLGB = full_logits(BASE)\nsumm(\"BASE (resim)\", LG=LGB)\nfor layer in (\"gru2\", \"gru1\"):\n    for dlt in (-0.5, +0.5):\n        Wd = variant({layer + \"f.biz\": (lambda b, d=dlt: b + d), layer + \"b.biz\": (lambda b, d=dlt: b + d)})\n        summ(\"%s z-bias %+.1f\" % (layer, dlt), LG=full_logits(Wd))\n```"}], "container": null, "stop_reason": null, "stop_sequence": null, "stop_details": null, "usage": {"input_tokens": 4, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 1513, "cache_read_input_tokens": 79965, "cache_creation": {"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens": 0, "ephemeral_1h_input_tokens": 1513}, "output_tokens": 8, "service_tier": "standard", "inference_geo": "global", "speed": "standard"}, "input_transformations": []