le-swap disagreement (mean |b| ≈ 0.7–0.8 logits in ambiguous frames, vs 0.25–0.4 for the y-mirror) — a non-equivariance that the view averaging already handles and that no bias-type edit can remove.\n\nOne last mechanistic hypothesis for the under-splitting: the recurrent states are too sticky (update gates `z` hold too long), so short possessions never register. If true, lowering the update-gate bias should add possessions and raise spellF1, and raising it should do the opposite. I'll test this as a two-sided sensitivity measurement in the simulator, separately for each GRU layer.\n\n```python\ndef full_logits(Wd):\n    out = {}\n    for n in NAMES:\n        X = views(D[n][\"x\"])\n        out[n] = back_end(front_end(X, Wd), Wd).astype(np.float32)\n    return out\ndef variant(edits):\n    Wd = {k: BASE[k] for k in BASE}\n    for k, fn in edits.items():\n        Wd[k] = fn(BASE[k].copy())\n    return Wd\nLGB = full_logits(BASE)\nsumm(\"BASE (resim)\", LG=LGB)\nfor layer in (\"gru2\", \"gru1\"):\n    for dlt in (-0.5, +0.5):\n        Wd = variant({layer + \"f.biz\": (lambda b, d=dlt: b + d), layer + \"b.biz\": (lambda b, d=dlt: b + d)})\n        summ(\"%s z-bias %+.1f\" % (layer, dlt), LG=full_logits(Wd))\n```", "ttft_ms": 31365, "type": "result", "duration_ms": 36671, "ttft_stream_ms": 1983, "time_to_request_ms": 166, "first_content_frame_ms": 1984, "queued_turn_count": 0, "result_index": 0, "model_usage_since_last_result": {"claude-fable-5-2": {"inputTokens": 4, "outputTokens": 3126, "cacheReadInputTokens": 79965, "cacheCreationInputTokens": 1513, "webSearchRequests": 0, "costUSD": 0.165273, "contextWindow": 1000000, "maxOutputTokens": 128000, "thinkingTokens": 2516, "cacheCreationEphemeral5mInputTokens": 0, "cacheCreationEphemeral1hInputTokens": 1513, "canonicalModel": "claude-fable-5-2", "provider": "firstParty", "costBasis": "list"}}}
